    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8590",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.20.$\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\leq 0.8416 ) = 0.80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\geq 0.8416 ) = 1 - 0.80 = 0.20.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(-0.8416) = 0.20.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14165008/assets/2be6ef2420c8789a0ff94f4f9540533af4134690ebe0c04c50eb02f358dfa266.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.8416) & =0.20 \\\\ P(Z\\le -0.8416) & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required value of $z$ is $-0.8416.$",
